SpartaCSS — Third-Party Icon Attribution (Transitional)
========================================================

Status: Temporary compliance measure. Not a permanent statement about
SpartaCSS's iconography.

Purpose
-------

This NOTICE exists solely to satisfy the attribution conditions of the
MIT and ISC licenses for icon shapes currently shipping in
`src/modules/icons/sparta-icons.css` and `src/core/sparta-tokens.css`
that were found, on direct geometric comparison, to be derived from
Feather Icons or Lucide.

This document does NOT make that geometry permanently acceptable under
RedSpartan's independent-iconography policy. Per
[ADR-0003](docs/adr/0003-independent-iconography-system.md), RedSpartan
maintains an independent, original iconography system; the icons listed
below are third-party-derived shapes awaiting replacement, not an
endorsed part of that system. Each entry below is removed from this file
in the same change that integrates that icon's independently constructed
replacement into production. This file is expected to shrink to nothing
and then be deleted.

If a later provenance investigation confirms additional third-party
origin among the icons currently classified "unverified/presumed" in
[`docs/design/icon-provenance-inventory.md`](docs/design/icon-provenance-inventory.md),
those icons must be added here until they too are replaced.

See also: [`docs/design/icon-provenance-inventory.md`](docs/design/icon-provenance-inventory.md)
for the full classification and evidence behind every entry below.

